          This folder contains the following files:

          File Name                 Description

          btirpc_find.c      Find RPC devices on the network
          bticard_test.c     Test BTIDriver cards

          examp1.c           Example 1: Report BTIDriver devices
          examp2.c           Example 2: Toggling LED and DIO
          examp3.c           Example 3: Monitoring DIO
          examp4.c           Example 4: Displaying SysMon
          examp5.c           Example 5: Polling Eventlog for BIT

          Makefile           GNU Makefile for examples

          README             This document

          Refer to the end of this document for corrections,
          warnings, and additional information.



     INTRODUCTION

          The BTICard.h and libbtiCard.so files are the C
          language header and shared library for the BTICard
          Driver API.  With these files, the user can write
          applications that operate a BTIDriver compliant
          device.



     MAKEFILE

          All the example programs can be built by simply
          running the command 'make'.

          By default, the Makefile builds the examples without
          linking to libtirpc.  This produces examples that can
          only understand IPv4 addresses in the ballard.conf
          configuration file.  To allow IPv6 addresses to be used
          in ballard.conf, run the command 'make ipv6'.  See the
          IPV6 section below for additional details.

          To remove the built example programs, run the 'make
          clean' command.



     BTICard.h

          Applications written in the C language that use the
          BTICard Driver API library must incorporate the
          header file BTICard.h using the #include
          preprocessor directive.  Assuming the header file
          is in the current working directory or in the
          INCLUDE path, the following line must be added to
          the top of the application's source file:

          #include "BTICard.h"



     EXAMPLE PROGRAMS

          Examples are provided in C source code files and
          must be compiled on the target processor.  Many of
          the examples use the ncurses library to output to
          the terminal.  Most Linux distributions ship the
          ncurses runtime libraries, but may not ship the
          programming headers.  You may need to install the
          ncurses programming headers separately.



     IPV6

          A network connection to some BTIDriver network devices
          can use an IPv6 address.  This requires the ballard.conf
          file to have an entry of the form:

               <CARDNUM>,<IPV6_ADDRESS>

          In addition, The libtirpc library must be installed on the
          client, and the client program must be linked to the libtirpc
          library.  The resulting program will still recognize IPv4
          addresses.



     FUNCTION OVERVIEW

          Functions are described in detail in the Ballard
          API Reference Manuals for the individual protocols.



     CORRECTIONS, WARNINGS, AND ADDITIONAL INFORMATION

          There is no additional information.


